  "id": "COMPOUND:20134 - PROTEIN:5798",
  "verbalization": "Marsdekoiside A appears to have a shared target relationship with NH-6 through multiple indirect pathways. The drug targets Carboxylesterase 2, which is a target of 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, a compound that also targets NH-6. Similarly, Marsdekoiside A targets SNB-78, which is a target of the same compound, and both pathways ultimately lead to NH-6. This suggests that Marsdekoiside A may act through a common mechanism, possibly by inhibiting a key enzyme or interacting with a shared molecular target that ultimately leads to NH-6 activation. The evidence supports a potential role for Marsdekoiside A in modulating the activity of a downstream pathway that involves 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, which in turn targets NH-6. The consistent presence of this intermediate compound across different target relationships indicates a possible functional link between Marsdekoiside A and NH-6, likely through a shared regulatory mechanism.",
